%SIXMD 1
# @?D6LZ - COMPRESS 36 BIT WORD STREAMS

## @?OPTIONS

### @?-X - COMPRESS A DXR EXECUTABLE
VALIDATE AN UNCOMPRESSED DXR EXECUTABLE, COMPRESS ONLY ITS LOAD IMAGE, PRESERVE
ITS RELOCATION MAP AND TEXT METADATA, AND SET THE DXR COMPRESSED EXECUTABLE
FLAG.  THE OUTPUT USES A THREE WORD DXR2 HEADER.

## @?OPERANDS

### @?SOURCE FILE
INPUT FILE.

### @?DEST FILE
OUTPUT FILE.  SOURCE AND DESTINATION MUST BE DIFFERENT FILES.

## DESCRIPTION

WITHOUT -X, D6LZ COMPRESSES THE SOURCE AS A RAW STREAM OF 36 BIT WORDS.

WITH -X, D6LZ CREATES A COMPRESSED EXECUTABLE THAT THE DAIMOS EXEC LOADER
RECOGNIZES FROM THE EXPLICIT DXR COMPRESSED FLAG.  COMPRESSION IS NEVER
INFERRED FROM FILE CONTENT.

D6LZ USES A 128 WORD HISTORY WINDOW AND MATCH LENGTHS FROM 3 THROUGH 130 WORDS.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?0 - COMPRESSION SUCCEEDED
### @?1 - INVALID INPUT, OUTPUT ERROR, OR COMPRESSION FAILED
